A||N||3||88coupe||88 engine swap||||1||
Z||000000||88coupe||07-23-2000||12:23 PM||||I'm swapping a 6cyl from a complete donor car into my 88 4cyl coupe.  Both cars are coupes, automatics, and have A/C.  I know I have to swapping the computer and engine wiring.  Do I have to swap every other wire in the car?  I have the engines out and left the A/C compressors in and hooked up.  However, I see that the mounting brackets and the compressors are quite different.  Would a bracket off an 88 6cyl accept my existing 88 compressor and bolt to the 86 engine?  Also since the cradles are quite different, the front engine mounts are in slightly different positions.  I think I can modify the mounts to fit, but would an 88 6cyl engine mounting bracket bolt onto the 4cyl mounting block?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||07-23-2000||01:06 PM||||I think that by 86 the wiring harnesses were all standardized, so if your donor is an 86 you should be able to just swap the engine compartment harness, and leave the body harness alone.<P>Jon<P>------------------<BR>'86 GT 3800<BR>'87 GT<BR>Rossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||07-23-2000||01:34 PM||||I did the exact same swap. You don't have to change all the wires just plug the new computer in and you are all set. I had to drill 2 holes for the front engine mount and the engine seems to be mounted solid. You will have to cut the coolant pipe that runs along the back of the engine so it clears the 88 suspension. Good luck any ? just ask me. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000003||pherder||07-23-2000||01:38 PM||||88coupe,<P>Don't forget to change out the fuel pump!<P>The V6 needs ~45 pounds where the L4 pump only supplies ~15 pounds.<P><P>------------------<BR>Paul, Sedgwick, KS<BR>88 Coupe, 88 Formula, 88 GT||||reg||1
